  "description": "Whether a catalogue entry's emulator loads a game's updates and add-on content from files in folders, which folders, and whether the asked content's own folder is one of them.",
  "vectors": [
    {
      "name": "extra-content-eden-scans-its-game-folder-and-its-external-folder",
      "rationale": "Eden registers updates and add-ons from .nsp and .xci packages in its external content folders, scanned at its start with every subfolder, and - ext_content_from_game_dirs being on by default - in its game folders, scanned only at their top without deep_scan and by a thread the launch does not wait for. The SDMC row is installed content, not a folder. The content lies directly in a game folder, so a package beside it is scanned.",
